{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>and the sailors saw</b> — the ship's counselors, like <i>your sailors and your pilots</i>. And Yefet said: for they were salt-merchants." "<b>to the farthest part of the ship</b> — to one farthest part of the ship, like <i>and he was buried in the cities of Gilead</i>." "<b>and he lay down and fell asleep</b> — from the sea's distress and its fury. Perhaps he had never before boarded a ship."], :book :jonah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The Yefet comment reads מוליכים, which I render literally; the word is obscure in this context and may be textually suspect.", 1 "Ibn Ezra cites an example of the singular used where the plural form appears; the parallel is to the construct ירכתי functioning distributively."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Jonah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=19&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:07:00.430993355Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}